think Kumara is heavily developed (494 files) so I ran an Explore survey first rather than build blind — it found the crypto seam (tally/kumara.rye, Ed25519 keypair/sign/verify) exists but the ledger record shapes (tilaks) do not; the load-bearing pair is point + bind
think built kumara/tilak.rye on the seam — the point tilak (a number in an Azimuth-tiered scarcity shape galaxy/star/planet, its keeper, a version that climbs by one) and the bind tilak (key married to keeper, signed both ways: the key signs the keeper's pubkey, the keeper signs the key's pubkey; neither alone is the identity, the mutual signature is)
think TAME throughout — Rye structs with explicit u32 widths, named ceilings (galaxy_ceiling 2^8, star_ceiling 2^16), contract asserts on seat/version/parent; the crypto reaches through the one seam
think a template is the shape, an instance one filled quintet; the module builds+verifies an instance from two seeds and emits Bron facts, never inventing a real pilot's key — the example uses plain seeds 0x11../0x22.., the maintainer fills his own by hand
obs caught two bugs — the point's keeper was the identity key not the keeper key (fixed to keeper_pubkey), and emit wrote data to stderr; refactored emit to stdout via std.Io.File.stdout writeStreamingAll (mirroring Rishi's say), diagnostics stay on stderr
obs witnessed GREEN — selftest proves the bind verifies both ways and a tampered bind refuses; the Rishi witness drives the built module and checks the Bron facts using the new find primitive (both 64-byte sigs present, point keeper matches bind keeper)
obs tame_style_check clean on kumara/tilak.rye; the example instance is 18 lines of valid Bron (point fact + bind fact)
obs held for Keaton's word — the settlement ledger (Sui or Grain-native), the final scarcity tiering, the rotation/capability/sponsor tilaks, and the human-name custody park are the JARL journeys past this one
